 {"id":"lem-convergent-implies-bounded","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"literature-derived","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch3.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter Proposition 3.19 states exactly that every convergent real sequence is bounded, and its proof uses epsilon=1, the triangle inequality, and a maximum over the finitely many initial terms, the same argument used here with the harmless 0-based indexing adjustment.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
