+{"id":"thm-squeeze","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"literature-derived","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch3.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter Theorem 3.23 states the squeeze theorem with pointwise bracketing. The item makes the standard finite-tail strengthening from pointwise to eventual bracketing. Its epsilon proof follows the sourced sandwich proof with a common threshold. The stale NKU URL redirected to a canonical websites.nku.edu URL that the model-side A4 check could not fetch on 2026-08-04, so it was omitted.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
 {"id":"lem-limit-abs","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch3.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter Corollary 3.25 states that x_n to x implies |x_n| to |x| and proves it by the reverse triangle inequality. The item adds the reverse implication at x=0 and the precise warning that the reverse fails away from zero, so it is a standard result with an added boundary clause.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
-{"id":"def-divergence-to-infinity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch3.pdf","https://www.nku.edu/~longa/classes/2011fall/mat420/days/highlights/highlights2.1.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter Definition 3.12 and the NKU notes give the same quantified definition of divergence to positive and negative infinity and explicitly distinguish it from convergence. The library uses 0-based indices, a weak threshold k>=K instead of n>N, and adds unboundedness/convergence consequences, so the construction is semantically identical but not textually exact.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
